    "body": "The saved Context3610 move changed Cue observations but the frozen Cue table cancelled their score effect. This adds an offline construction that holds that Context move fixed and learns only the existing shared Cue coefficients, using saved native states and the original selected-parent gate. Serving code has no new cases or target-dependent routing.\n\nOne aggregate from eighteen streamed Cue backward calls drives one frozen960-coordinate pass;95 current-intermediate-CE proposals are accepted. Full physical aliases, earliest BASE donor, donor-dependent bridge/Generate, and fixed U are scored before every decision. Actual fractional masters are preserved and coherent Source/Cue/Prefix/U export independently reloads all eighteen pools.\n\nThe candidate remains negative and unselected: combined CE4.391651926613631→3.4856878825004602 and task probability298710449/16027151659→298196418/6346398572 improve, but original reference winners fall17→16. Row4 position4target92 loses to471. The task donor reaches the expected Source while its wrong offset307 still beats267. Identical within-Source Cue incidence leaves those direct score gaps unchanged. Original parent masters are restored; no autoregressive/full512 evaluation or useful-language claim follows.\n\nValidation at measured sourcef763d02: scoped formatting,79 example tests and CUDA release build PASS; mathematical/adversarial exact-source review PASS. Independent saved readerda02ce7d audits raw18 gradient aggregation, frozen960 ordering/native transactions, master packing/bindings and18 reloaded pools PASS11.767185s. Full Rust report complete-file verification PASS. Runtime187f27d924e3c30d74898d1ba8c3888cbaa87020 and complete result324e9b82f69bd457c73f214f0aa643e895833457 are privately preserved with fresh download/hash verification. Exact finalhead6f8461dbc226d1b3237eeada7bf739848d057412 source/evidence review PASS; finalhead checks are being posted before queue admission.\n\nNext dependency after protected delivery is a saved Prefix/U margin and global shared-key discriminator with the newly retained per-term Cue gradients. Prefix learning remains NOT_ADMITTED pending that evidence and prospective card. Other labs’ main changes are integrated and preserved. All new work is pod-only below the local disk floor.\n\nReferences #820.",
